+## 11. Kimi-K3 atomic checkpoint bundles (offline)
+
+For a checkpoint interval of K tokens, register `block_size=K` and `linear_step=1`.
+The full group charges all MLA KV for that segment; the linear group charges all
+KDA SSM and convolution state at its endpoint. The pair is one indivisible LRU
+object. The trace keys must identify prefix chains, and a finer trace block size
+may be coarsened to K. Coarsening cannot create intermediate state checkpoints.
+The core Fenwick tree, RLE format and capacity projector are unchanged.
+
+Set top-level `reserve_last_token=true` when a serving request must recompute at
+least one prompt token to produce logits. The runner clips only the published
+Facts hit curve to `floor((input_len - 1) / K)` complete objects. It preserves the
+original input length and submits every complete input object to the LRU,
+including a last object excluded from the current hit. The default is `false`.
+
+For the included Kimi-K3 example, K=1024 and TP8 with BF16 MLA/conv and FP32 SSM
+produce a 675,864,576-byte bundle over all eight ranks. Capacity inputs named
+`capacity_gb` by the historical CLI are GiB (`2^30` bytes), counting stored tensor
+payload, not allocator/index overhead. See the [workflow SOP](../tools/kimi_k3_capacity/SOP.md)
+for model-config-derived byte formulas, actual Facts/query commands and HiSim
+capacity experiments. These are explicitly modeled checkpoint bundles; default
+SGLang Mamba dual-pool eviction and actual GPU latency are separate validations.
